{
	"name": "Paritor",
	"type": "feature",
	"img": "icons/sundries/flags/banner-white.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<p>You have learned to not merely protect those you swear to defend, but work with them, achieving together that which would be more difficult alone. You gain the following benefits:</p><ul><li><p>Your Strength, Dexterity, or Constitution score increases by 1, to a maximum of 20.</p></li><li><p>Your exertion pool increases by 1.</p></li><li><p>You gain an additional combat maneuver of a degree you could learn. It does not count against your maneuvers known.</p></li><li><p>You and your defensive targets treat the AC of your offensive targets as if it were 1 lower than it is and deal an additional 1d6 points of damage to it with weapon attacks. If a weapon attack deals more than one type of damage, you choose what type of damage gets the +1d6 bonus.</p></li></ul><p>Once you have taken this feat, you can no longer gain levels in non-champion classes.</p>",
